            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p17-q21-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\dfrac{1}{1+\\cos\\theta}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", for ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\sin\\theta\\ne0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p17-q21-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\sin^2\\theta=(1-\\cos\\theta)(1+\\cos\\theta)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and cancel the common factor.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The original LHS requires $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$, so $1-\\cos\\theta$ and $1+\\cos\\theta$ are both nonzero.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1-\\cos\\theta}{\\sin^2\\theta}&=\\frac{1-\\cos\\theta}{1-\\cos^2\\theta}\\\\\\frac{1-\\cos\\theta}{\\sin^2\\theta}&=\\frac{1-\\cos\\theta}{(1-\\cos\\theta)(1+\\cos\\theta)}\\\\\\frac{1-\\cos\\theta}{\\sin^2\\theta}&=\\frac{1}{1+\\cos\\theta}\\end{align*}$$\nThe final expression is the RHS.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q20-25-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$2\\cos^2\\theta-1=1-2\\sin^2\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
