              {
                "id": "p17-q25-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Factor and use ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "1-2\\sin^2\\theta=2\\cos^2\\theta-1",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " to cancel the common factor.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The original denominator requires $\\cos\\theta\\ne0$ and $2\\cos^2\\theta-1\\ne0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\sin\\theta-2\\sin^3\\theta}{2\\cos^3\\theta-\\cos\\theta}&=\\frac{\\sin\\theta(1-2\\sin^2\\theta)}{\\cos\\theta(2\\cos^2\\theta-1)}\\\\\\frac{\\sin\\theta-2\\sin^3\\theta}{2\\cos^3\\theta-\\cos\\theta}&=\\frac{\\sin\\theta(2\\cos^2\\theta-1)}{\\cos\\theta(2\\cos^2\\theta-1)}\\\\\\frac{\\sin\\theta-2\\sin^3\\theta}{2\\cos^3\\theta-\\cos\\theta}&=\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\\\\\\frac{\\sin\\theta-2\\sin^3\\theta}{2\\cos^3\\theta-\\cos\\theta}&=\\tan\\theta\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $\\sin^2\\theta=1-\\cos^2\\theta$, the final expression is the RHS.",
